- How would you adapt for a streaming pipeline or very large data that doesn't fit in memory?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to convert dependency graphs into scheduling via topological order; checks understanding of longest-path DP on DAG, cycle detection, and clear complexity analysis.

## Key Concepts
- Topological sort (Kahn / DFS)
- DAG longest path DP
- Cycle detection
- Complexity analysis

## Code Example

```javascript
function earliestFinishTimes(n, edges, durations) {
  const adj = Array.from({ length: n }, () => []);
  const indeg = Array(n).fill(0);
  for (const [u, v] of edges) { adj[u].push(v); indeg[v]++; }
  const q = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) if (indeg[i] === 0) q.push(i);
  const finish = durations.slice();
  let seen = 0;
  while (q.length) {
    const u = q.shift();
    seen++;
    for (const v of adj[u]) {
      finish[v] = Math.max(finish[v], finish[u] + durations[v]);
      if (--indeg[v] === 0) q.push(v);
    }
  }
  if (seen !== n) throw new Error('Cycle detected');
  return finish;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for multiple start times or optional prerequisites?
- How does the solution change if edge weights represent communication delay instead of task duration?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests mastery of graph algorithms, state expansion techniques, and path reconstruction under constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Dijkstra's algorithm on expanded state space (node, used)
- Edge relaxation with and without discount application
- Path reconstruction across state transitions

## Code Example
```javascript
function shortestWithDiscounts(n, edges, s, t, K) {
  const adj = Array.from({length: n}, ()=>[]);
  for(const [u,v,w] of edges){ adj[u].push([v,w]); }
  const INF = Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
  const dist = Array.from({length: n}, ()=> Array(K+1).fill(INF));
  const prev = Array.from({length: n}, ()=> Array(K+1).fill(null));

  const pq = new MinHeap();
  dist[s][0] = 0;
  pq.insert([s,0,0]); // [node, used, distance]

  while(!pq.isEmpty()){
    const [u,used,d] = pq.extractMin();
    if(d > dist[u][used]) continue;
    if(u === t) break;

    for(const [v,w] of adj[u]){
      // Without discount
      if(d + w < dist[v][used]){
        dist[v][used] = d + w;
        prev[v][used] = [u,used];
        pq.insert([v,used,d+w]);
      }
      // With discount if available
      if(used < K && d < dist[v][used+1]){
        dist[v][used+1] = d;
        prev[v][used+1] = [u,used];
        pq.insert([v,used+1,d]);
      }
    }
  }

  // Find optimal state at target
  let minDist = INF, minUsed = -1;
  for(let k=0;k<=K;k++){
    if(dist[t][k] < minDist){
      minDist = dist[t][k];
      minUsed = k;
    }
  }

  // Path reconstruction
  const path = [];
  let curr = [t,minUsed];
  while(curr && prev[curr[0]][curr[1]]){
    path.unshift(curr[0]);
    curr = prev[curr[0]][curr[1]];
  }
  if(curr[0] === s) path.unshift(s);

  return {distance: minDist, path};
}
```

## Edge Cases
- Unreachable target: return INF distance
- K=0: reduces to standard Dijkstra
- K larger than path length: effectively unlimited discounts
- Multiple optimal states: choose minimal used count

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates combined data structures and time-based eviction. Tests ability to design per-key streaming aggregates with real-time top-K, using arrays/linked lists/hashtable/heap and lazy deletions.

## Key Concepts
- Sliding window aggregation; - Hash maps for per-tag buckets; - Deques for per-tag event queues; - Max-heap with lazy invalidation for top-K.

## Code Example
```javascript
class SlidingTagTopK {
  constructor(windowMs){ this.W=windowMs; this.tagMap=new Map(); this.heap=[]; this.ver=0; }
  _expire(tag, now){ const b=this.tagMap.get(tag); while (b.queue.length && b.queue[0].ts <= now - this.W){ b.sum -= b.queue.shift().val; } }
  addEvent(tag, userId, value, ts){ let b=this.tagMap.get(tag); if(!b){ b={sum:0, queue:[], ver:0}; this.tagMap.set(tag,b);} this._expire(tag, ts); b.queue.push({ts, val: value}); b.sum += value; this.ver++; // push new entry
    this._heapPush({sum: b.sum, tag, ver:this.ver}); }
  topK(K){ // lazy
    const res=[]; const seen=new Set(); while (res.length<K && this.heap.length){ const top=this._heapPop(); if (top.ver===this.tagMap.get(top.tag).ver){ res.push(top.tag); seen.add(top.tag); } }
    return res;
  }
}
```

